---
// Code call tree mapped directly to pprof top `flat` vs `cum` numbers and Flame Graph widths.
const W = 900;
const H = 286;
---
<figure class="gpfc">
  <div class="gpfc-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Trace linking Go call hierarchy handleRequest -> parseJSON -> bytes.Split directly to pprof flat versus cumulative columns and horizontal Flame Graph box widths.">
      {/* Left panel: Call tree + pprof top numbers */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="440" height="258" rx="10" class="gpfc-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gpfc-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Call stack -&gt; pprof top (Flat vs. Cum columns)</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Ngăn xếp gọi hàm -&gt; Bảng pprof top (Flat vs. Cum)</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="58" width="408" height="58" rx="6" class="gpfc-box" />
      <text x="44" y="79" class="gpfc-code">handleRequest()  -&gt; Flat=2%   Cum=100%  (wrapper only)</text>
      <text x="44" y="99" class="gpfc-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Low Flat because it delegates almost all CPU down to callees.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Flat thấp vì chỉ làm hàm điều phối, đẩy việc xuống các hàm con.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="128" width="408" height="58" rx="6" class="gpfc-box" />
      <text x="44" y="149" class="gpfc-code">parsePayload()   -&gt; Flat=14%  Cum=98%   (loop + calls)</text>
      <text x="44" y="169" class="gpfc-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Sorting strictly by Flat hides parsePayload; sort -cum sees it first!</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Nếu chỉ lọc theo Flat dễ bỏ sót caller nóng này; phải xem cả -cum!</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="198" width="408" height="58" rx="6" class="gpfc-box is-red" />
      <text x="44" y="219" class="gpfc-b-red">bytes.Split() + runtime.mallocgc -&gt; Flat=84%  Cum=84%</text>
      <text x="44" y="239" class="gpfc-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Leaf bottleneck! Optimizing parsePayload caller cuts 84% leaf churn.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Nút thắt lá! Sửa cách parsePayload gọi nó là cắt ngay 84% chi phí.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right panel: Flame Graph width reading */}
      <rect x="470" y="14" width="416" height="258" rx="10" class="gpfc-card" />
      <text x="486" y="42" class="gpfc-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. Reading Flame Graphs: Look for WIDE plateaus, NOT tall spires</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Đọc Flame Graph: Tìm BỤC RỘNG, đừng bị đánh lừa bởi THÁP CAO</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="486" y="186" width="384" height="32" rx="4" class="gpfc-box" />
      <text x="678" y="206" text-anchor="middle" class="gpfc-code">handleRequest (Width = 100% Cum samples)</text>

      <rect x="486" y="148" width="376" height="32" rx="4" class="gpfc-box" />
      <text x="674" y="168" text-anchor="middle" class="gpfc-code">parsePayload (98% Cum width; ~14% uncovered top)</text>

      <rect x="486" y="110" width="322" height="32" rx="4" class="gpfc-box is-red" />
      <text x="647" y="130" text-anchor="middle" class="gpfc-b-red">bytes.Split / mallocgc (84% WIDE ROOFTOP!)</text>

      <rect x="486" y="64" width="384" height="34" rx="6" class="gpfc-box is-ok" />
      <text x="678" y="85" text-anchor="middle" class="gpfc-b-ok">Y-axis = Stack Depth (no meaning!) | X-axis = Total % Samples</text>

      <text x="486" y="242" class="gpfc-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Note: X-axis is alphabetical % — NOT chronological time!</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Trục X xếp theo % mẫu &amp; A–Z (KHÔNG phải thứ tự thời gian).</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Top frames uncovered at the roof of a Flame Graph equal Flat self-time, while the full box span underneath represents Cumulative (Cum) time. Wide flat plateaus point straight to real Level-2/3 targets.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Phần nóc lộ thiên trên Flame Graph chính là Flat self-time, còn cả chiều rộng thanh bên dưới là tổng Cum (gồm cả hàm con). Mọi bục rộng chính là mỏ vàng để tối ưu.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gpfc { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gpfc-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gpfc svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 680px; height: auto; }
  .gpfc text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gpfc-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gpfc-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gpfc-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gpfc-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gpfc-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gpfc-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gpfc-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gpfc-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gpfc-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gpfc-code { font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: 11px; fill: var(--text); }
  .gpfc-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .gpfc figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
